<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 21 May, from 1502 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1502 CE <span class="tih-ago">524 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Portuguese navigator João da Nova sights St Helena</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Returning from India, João da Nova's fleet found an uninhabited island in the South Atlantic, traditionally on St Helena's feast day. It became a vital supply stop and later Napoleon's place of exile.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1674 CE <span class="tih-ago">352 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Sobieski is elected King of Poland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The nobility of the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth elected the victorious commander Jan Sobieski as John III. In 1683 he led the relief army that broke the Ottoman siege of Vienna.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1840 CE <span class="tih-ago">186 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Hobson proclaims British sovereignty over New Zealand</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Following the Treaty of Waitangi, Lieutenant-Governor Hobson declared British sovereignty over the North Island by cession and the South Island by discovery. The treaty's meaning is still central to New Zealand law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1881 CE <span class="tih-ago">145 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Clara Barton founds the American Red Cross</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Clara Barton, a nurse in the Civil War, set up the American Association of the Red Cross in Washington. It became the country's main organisation for disaster relief and blood donation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1927 CE <span class="tih-ago">99 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lindbergh lands in Paris after flying the Atlantic alone</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles Lindbergh touched down at Le Bourget after 33.5 hours in the air, greeted by a crowd of some 100,000. He won the $25,000 Orteig Prize and instant worldwide fame.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1991 CE <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rajiv Gandhi is assassinated in Tamil Nadu</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A suicide bomber from the Tamil Tigers killed the former Indian prime minister at an election rally in Sriperumbudur. His mother, Indira Gandhi, had been assassinated in 1984.</p></div></li></ol>
